  Changes worth knowing about
  - Dev database: I applied migration 0124 to your local dev database. It only adds the two new user columns.
  - Translations: the new UI text is English only, as you chose. The i18n sync check now reports 28 keys missing in each of the 18 other languages. Its CI check only runs on preview, so PRs
    into dev won't fail, but merging into preview will until they're translated.
  - Profile updates can't touch 2FA: I marked the two new fields read-only on the profile-update endpoint. Without that, PATCH /api/users/me/ could have switched 2FA off with no code.
  - Email worker: I listed the email task explicitly in CELERY_IMPORTS, because sign-in can't finish without that email being sent.
  - Shared helper: maskEmail now lives in @plane/utils, since the web and admin apps both use it.

  Two gaps outside the design
  - Email change bypasses 2FA: an existing endpoint, users/me/email/, lets someone with a signed-in session change the account email using only a code sent to the new address. They could then
    receive the 2FA codes, or reset the password. This isn't part of the 2FA work, but it's worth a follow-up.
  - Email flooding: someone who knows the password can make a code email go out on every sign-in attempt. Guessing the code itself is capped (5 tries per code, a lock after 10 failures in 30
    minutes), but nothing limits how often the first code is sent.